WEBVTT

01:45.105 --> 01:48.775
He went up there!
He's promoting himself too!

01:49.359 --> 01:51.528
I appreciate your ardent friendship.

01:51.611 --> 01:55.782
I knew I was taking a gamble
when I introduced you,

01:55.865 --> 01:58.284
but to be honest, I was in a cold sweat.

01:58.368 --> 02:01.287
If you didn't cooperate and come up here,

02:01.913 --> 02:04.791
I'd be getting thrashed right about now.

02:05.750 --> 02:07.544
I honestly appreciate this.

02:09.129 --> 02:10.171
Hey!

02:10.255 --> 02:12.715
What the hell's going on here, Mr. Kaiser?

02:13.758 --> 02:17.178
This ain't your ring. It's mine.

02:20.390 --> 02:22.392
Hear that?

02:22.475 --> 02:25.311
Get outta this ring
before you're thrown out.

02:25.395 --> 02:27.188
What an odd thing to say.

02:27.272 --> 02:33.111
You're a former world champion
and still a superstar, Andrei Valev.

02:33.194 --> 02:36.322
You blessed this ring
with your 31st KO victory.

02:36.906 --> 02:39.576
Everyone here celebrates you.

02:40.577 --> 02:42.579
Except for this man.

02:43.163 --> 02:45.582
This man came here to insult you!

02:45.665 --> 02:51.087
No, in fact, he came to trample
on boxing itself, not just you.

02:52.547 --> 02:55.717
Kaiser, that little man with that body?

02:55.800 --> 02:58.052
How's he gonna insult me?

03:00.555 --> 03:02.473
There is a saying in Japan.

03:03.057 --> 03:06.477
"The bigger the man,
the smaller the brain."

03:07.854 --> 03:09.898
You Americans wouldn't understand this.

03:10.565 --> 03:14.777
The intellect of someone like you, who
only sees the body as a mass of muscle,

03:14.861 --> 03:19.240
wouldn't understand martial arts
nurtured over an eternity of 4,000 years.

03:20.783 --> 03:23.995
Mr. Retsu,
this isn't a pro wrestling ring.

03:24.579 --> 03:27.582
Your blatant taunts
won't start any trouble.

03:28.082 --> 03:31.753
Retsu, I've prepared a demonstration
for you to exhibit your stuff.

03:34.505 --> 03:38.676
To you, it's a stupid little performance,

03:38.760 --> 03:41.971
but it'll make it easier
to understand for Americans.

03:42.055 --> 03:45.433
Just show them a fragment
of that eternity.

03:46.142 --> 03:47.268
Mr. Kaiser.

03:48.519 --> 03:51.272
I thought that you were
a talented promoter.

03:51.773 --> 03:55.443
Who would be entertained
if I destroyed this?

03:56.778 --> 03:58.363
Isn't there something else here

03:59.364 --> 04:04.035
that's larger, tougher
and more worthy of being destroyed?

04:06.037 --> 04:07.705
R... Retsu...

04:15.296 --> 04:18.549
Karate was the start
of my career in punching people.

04:19.050 --> 04:23.471
If you'd like, I'd be glad to fight you
bare-knuckled, Mr. Retsu.

04:24.055 --> 04:25.348
Kick his ass, Valev!

04:25.431 --> 04:27.725
Split him right down the middle!

04:34.065 --> 04:35.692
It's been turned to powder!

04:35.775 --> 04:37.235
He didn't break them.

04:37.902 --> 04:39.737
He turned the blocks to sand.

04:43.825 --> 04:47.745
This is war! Dragon versus Goliath.

04:48.329 --> 04:50.873
The greatest and most glorious in history.

04:50.957 --> 04:53.710
An unprecedented exhibition match!

04:55.086 --> 05:00.258
Mr. Retsu, can you tell us about
your history and your career as a fighter?

05:01.050 --> 05:03.511
I'm not quite sure how to explain it.

05:04.178 --> 05:06.639
I entered the Bailin Temple
at the age of four.

05:06.723 --> 05:09.517
After that, I spent my days training.

05:10.518 --> 05:12.520
What about your fight history?

05:13.146 --> 05:15.106
I don't have an official match record.

05:15.606 --> 05:18.026
All of my fights have been unofficial.

05:20.361 --> 05:23.531
Then what's your record
for those unofficial fights?

05:23.614 --> 05:25.658
I've never counted them,

05:26.409 --> 05:28.870
neither those that I've won nor lost.

05:29.370 --> 05:31.289
What were the rules?

05:31.873 --> 05:32.790
Rules?

05:32.874 --> 05:35.793
I doubt they were boxing rules.

05:35.877 --> 05:36.836
They were fights.

05:37.378 --> 05:39.797
That is, a comparison of strength.

05:40.590 --> 05:44.052
You mean they were
mixed martial arts rules?

05:44.135 --> 05:45.553
Mixed martial arts?

05:45.636 --> 05:47.055
- What?
- How does he not know?

05:47.638 --> 05:50.475
I've never been in a match
governed by rules.

05:50.558 --> 05:53.561
They were just about
seeing who was stronger.

05:54.145 --> 05:56.064
If I may ask, what happened to your leg?

05:57.148 --> 05:59.442
I lost it in a fight with a friend.

06:00.985 --> 06:01.819
You're kidding.

06:01.903 --> 06:03.821
That sort of thing happens.

06:04.614 --> 06:06.824
That is the nature of a fight.

06:07.492 --> 06:09.577
I have a question for Mr. Kaiser.

06:09.660 --> 06:12.330
What will the rules be for this fight?

06:13.289 --> 06:16.793
Two men will compete
using the strength of their fists.

06:16.876 --> 06:18.336
That's the rule.

06:18.419 --> 06:21.089
Then wouldn't you say that's boxing?

06:22.673 --> 06:26.803
I'll let you decide
how you define the rules.

06:26.886 --> 06:29.097
This is simply an exhibition, after all.

06:29.180 --> 06:31.349
You call it an exhibition,

06:31.432 --> 06:33.851
but one of them's a former world champion.

06:33.935 --> 06:37.230
Look, I just promote matches.

06:37.313 --> 06:39.857
I just present them to you.

06:40.483 --> 06:45.238
Like, "Here is a fight between beasts.
If you wanna come watch, be my guest."

06:55.873 --> 06:59.127
A boxing match
with the former champion, Valev?

06:59.210 --> 07:01.879
That's pretty amazing, Retsu.

07:04.590 --> 07:06.384
Your debut match is with Valev?

07:09.262 --> 07:10.388
You're disrespectful.

07:11.681 --> 07:12.890
I am not disrespectful.

07:12.974 --> 07:15.768
You're disrespecting boxing.

07:17.228 --> 07:19.772
Your career consists
of just two sparring matches.

07:20.356 --> 07:23.776
Do you think you're a world champion now?

07:25.361 --> 07:29.532
This is a good chance. If you can see
a punch from this oldster, dodge...

07:32.368 --> 07:35.288
What's the matter, Bruce Lee?

07:35.997 --> 07:40.293
Can't see a punch coming
from a boxer who retired ten years ago?

07:40.877 --> 07:43.296
That's how quick a jab from a boxer is.

07:43.880 --> 07:46.299
If I'd been Valev, you'd be dead!

07:47.383 --> 07:48.926
Turn down this fight.

07:49.010 --> 07:52.054
That would be the polite way
to treat the former champion.

07:52.638 --> 07:54.724
We've got no more business here in Vegas.

07:54.807 --> 07:56.809
We'll take a flight home tomorrow.

07:56.893 --> 08:00.021
I couldn't care less what Kaiser says.

08:00.104 --> 08:03.399
He's nothing but a promoter after... Huh?

08:04.942 --> 08:06.944
What the... Huh?

08:10.656 --> 08:11.491
Sorry.

08:14.160 --> 08:17.413
It seems I reflexively dislocated
your wrist.

08:17.914 --> 08:20.333
You mean you saw it?

08:20.416 --> 08:22.418
I didn't intend to dodge it.

08:23.544 --> 08:26.631
You've been in the boxing business
a long time, Mr. Fukamachi.

08:26.714 --> 08:28.841
Your anger is perfectly reasonable.

08:28.925 --> 08:33.095
That punch is my punishment
for hurting your feelings.

08:33.763 --> 08:39.393
However, I ask that you also understand
my feelings regarding martial arts.

08:41.229 --> 08:44.357
Well, it is just an exhibition.

08:44.941 --> 08:47.151
I guess I can stay a little while longer.

08:47.235 --> 08:48.069
Thank you!

08:51.113 --> 08:52.990
Chinese dragon!

08:53.074 --> 08:54.992
Chinese kung fu!

08:55.076 --> 08:55.993
Sea King!

08:59.247 --> 09:00.998
<i>Retsu was perplexed.</i>

09:01.916 --> 09:05.253
<i>It was his first fight
for public entertainment.</i>

09:06.128 --> 09:07.004
<i>Incomprehensible...</i>

09:08.214 --> 09:09.090
<i>Incomprehensible...</i>

09:10.216 --> 09:11.092
<i>Incomprehensible...</i>

09:12.260 --> 09:14.512
<i>Public entertainment is incomprehensible.</i>

09:25.106 --> 09:28.776
<i>Why is this man pretending to be angry?</i>

09:29.360 --> 09:32.280
<i>Even if it's for the sake
of entertainment,</i>

09:33.030 --> 09:35.283
<i>why is it necessary to go this far?</i>

09:35.366 --> 09:37.535
It's showtime!

09:38.119 --> 09:43.541
The great People's Republic of China
has bared its fangs to the world!

09:43.624 --> 09:44.542
<i>What a charade.</i>

09:44.625 --> 09:46.627
Unsatisfied with just the financial...

09:46.711 --> 09:48.796
<i>All these things are useless for a fight.</i>

09:48.879 --> 09:51.799
...expanding their influence
over the world of sport.

09:51.882 --> 09:54.302
<i>Even the spectators are acting.</i>

09:56.887 --> 09:58.306
Just try it!

09:58.389 --> 10:00.558
Try it If you think you can beat me!

10:00.641 --> 10:02.059
Way to go!

10:02.143 --> 10:04.061
Beat the crap outta him, Valev!

10:05.187 --> 10:06.480
<i>This is also an act.</i>

10:06.564 --> 10:08.608
<i>He kicked knowing he wouldn't hit me.</i>

10:09.400 --> 10:10.234
Come on.

10:14.655 --> 10:18.826
Mr. Retsu, my own showtime is over.

10:20.411 --> 10:21.245
Fight clean.

10:22.246 --> 10:24.081
From here on, this is a competition.

10:24.707 --> 10:26.584
No more acting.

10:27.668 --> 10:31.589
Retsu, don't you die.

10:38.679 --> 10:40.473
<i>He can move that quick?</i>

10:41.057 --> 10:42.975
<i>Height, 237 cm.</i>

10:44.560 --> 10:46.062
<i>Weight, 151 kilos.</i>

10:46.812 --> 10:49.106
<i>That's good footwork
for such a massive man.</i>

10:49.190 --> 10:50.483
<i>As I suspected.</i>

10:51.067 --> 10:53.569
<i>His fighting power
isn't simply his great size.</i>

10:53.653 --> 10:54.487
<i>In that case...</i>

10:55.446 --> 10:56.989
- Huh?
- What?

10:59.075 --> 11:01.243
Ah! You idiot!

11:02.370 --> 11:04.121
He's squatting in the corner!

11:04.205 --> 11:05.247
Has he given up?

11:08.501 --> 11:11.504
You've put yourself into a corner
while facing me.

11:12.088 --> 11:16.300
You just put yourself in the most
dangerous spot in the boxing ring.

11:16.384 --> 11:21.055
I'm certain that you, in your own way,
understand the meaning of this, right?

11:21.597 --> 11:23.891
Hey! What's the meaning of this?

11:25.935 --> 11:27.520
Stand up and fight!

11:28.187 --> 11:30.606
And what do you mean by "stand"?

11:31.399 --> 11:33.526
I am not sitting.

11:34.110 --> 11:37.279
Though my hips are low,
I most certainly am standing.

11:37.363 --> 11:40.282
And I don't understand
why you're telling me to fight.

11:41.909 --> 11:44.912
I have no intention of fighting Valev.

11:45.538 --> 11:48.541
I have no intention of punching him
or being punched by him.

11:49.125 --> 11:52.795
You're giving up the fight
without throwing a single jab?

11:52.878 --> 11:57.049
I'll win this
without throwing a single jab.

11:57.633 --> 12:00.052
Can you please get out of the way,
Mr. Mills?

12:00.136 --> 12:02.930
You're keeping me from beating this guy.

12:07.685 --> 12:09.854
<i>The giant Valev was delighted.</i>

12:10.646 --> 12:11.981
<i>He was encountering</i>

12:12.064 --> 12:15.151
<i>a mysterious fighting style
he had never before imagined.</i>

12:15.693 --> 12:18.404
<i>And he was delighted that most likely...</i>

12:18.487 --> 12:22.324
<i>no, most definitely,
he was going to smash through it.</i>

12:41.552 --> 12:43.095
<i>Musunkei</i>...

12:43.804 --> 12:49.226
<i>The last thing that Valev saw
was a single photographer.</i>

12:58.402 --> 13:00.988
Welcome, Sea King Retsu.

13:01.822 --> 13:07.161
This is your reward for your fight
last night, for that super technique.

13:07.828 --> 13:08.788
Mine?

13:09.413 --> 13:10.998
In a single night,

13:11.665 --> 13:15.503
you've become the most
sensational Chinese person in the U.S.

13:16.212 --> 13:19.757
My staff has been overwhelmed
with requests since early this morning.

13:20.758 --> 13:23.636
<i>It's no surprise.
Everyone all over the U.S. saw it.</i>

13:23.719 --> 13:27.598
<i>The motionless glove
that suddenly smashed through his face.</i>

13:35.231 --> 13:37.149
Tell us how you feel right now.

13:37.233 --> 13:39.485
I already knew this would happen.

13:39.568 --> 13:42.655
I simply displayed
the dominance of kung fu.

13:42.738 --> 13:44.240
For your finishing blow,

13:44.323 --> 13:48.160
you were just touching him like this
when you punched him.

13:48.244 --> 13:49.620
That's <i>Musunkei.</i>

13:49.703 --> 13:52.164
It can also be called the "No-Inch Punch."

13:52.248 --> 13:53.916
"No-Inch"?

13:53.999 --> 13:58.671
In any case,
your martial art, boxing, is still young.

14:00.005 --> 14:02.925
I want to show you a fight
of mature fighting skills

14:03.008 --> 14:05.636
against the next formidable foe,
as soon as possible.

14:08.722 --> 14:11.934
That one comment
turned the whole world against you.

14:12.518 --> 14:14.436
It's just like I told you, right?

14:14.520 --> 14:17.439
You'll be showered
in dozens of millions of dollars

14:17.523 --> 14:20.943
and there'll be monsters
that'll make you wanna run away.

14:21.026 --> 14:23.696
Here, take it with you.

14:23.779 --> 14:25.281
How much is there?

14:25.781 --> 14:27.616
In dollars, it's two million.

14:27.700 --> 14:30.035
In weight, it's 20 kilos.

14:31.036 --> 14:32.788
I got you an attaché case.

14:32.872 --> 14:34.456
It should fit just right.

14:34.540 --> 14:35.541
I see.

14:36.125 --> 14:39.545
I don't know by what contrivance
this wealth was created,

14:39.628 --> 14:41.714
but if you want me to have it, I will.

14:41.797 --> 14:43.257
But what are those?

14:44.300 --> 14:47.720
Those filthy boots next to my money.

14:54.101 --> 14:55.603
Don't tell me to take it.

14:55.686 --> 14:58.439
You'll be putting it
in the case and handing it to me.

14:58.522 --> 15:01.942
If you don't, then I'll shatter
those impolite feet of yours.

15:05.654 --> 15:06.822
Thank you.

15:07.698 --> 15:09.617
I've called a car for you.

15:10.326 --> 15:11.619
I appreciate it.

15:14.705 --> 15:17.583
Would you like a brandy, Mr. Retsu?

15:19.084 --> 15:20.920
No. Oolong tea.

15:21.712 --> 15:24.715
Sorry... I can only offer Fauchon black tea.

15:27.718 --> 15:30.804
These limousines sure are useless.

15:35.726 --> 15:37.728
DIE SCUM - MAMA'S BOY

15:49.990 --> 15:52.159
<i>What? Now?</i>

15:54.244 --> 15:55.746
This isn't any good.

15:56.246 --> 15:58.666
I need another cup.

15:59.249 --> 16:02.336
But would he really come so suddenly?

16:02.920 --> 16:05.172
<i>He's never been here even once before.</i>

16:07.758 --> 16:11.095
<i>He's close. I can tell he's really close!</i>

16:11.845 --> 16:14.181
<i>Twenty meters away? No, even closer.</i>

16:14.765 --> 16:15.766
<i>Ten meters?</i>

16:16.517 --> 16:18.185
<i>Wait. Even closer?</i>

16:18.268 --> 16:20.688
<i>Don't tell me he's already at the door.</i>

16:20.771 --> 16:22.940
<i>I doubt he's gotten that far...</i>

16:23.023 --> 16:24.817
<i>What?!</i>

16:24.900 --> 16:26.443
Hi. Welcome.

16:29.780 --> 16:30.948
It's Blue Mountain.

16:31.031 --> 16:32.533
This sure is sudden.

16:33.826 --> 16:37.705
You know, I kinda thought you'd come,
so I made two cups.

16:38.288 --> 16:40.791
I guess it shows we're related, right?

16:44.044 --> 16:47.464
<i>Whoa! He's actually drinking the coffee!</i>

16:49.383 --> 16:50.968
You want any sugar?

16:52.136 --> 16:52.970
Is this it?

16:54.054 --> 16:57.558
Is this the father-son relationship
that you're after?

17:04.732 --> 17:07.317
Well, I guess this is about right.

17:09.570 --> 17:10.571
<i>Is it gonna happen?</i>

17:12.406 --> 17:13.991
<i>Turning the table...</i>

17:14.074 --> 17:15.909
Are you frightened of your father?

17:18.579 --> 17:21.290
I doubt there's been a single second

17:21.373 --> 17:25.502
that I haven't been afraid of my father,
afraid of Yujiro Hanma.

17:29.631 --> 17:32.009
Fear. Tremors.

17:32.092 --> 17:36.180
Adoration. Admiration. Respect.

17:36.847 --> 17:39.600
And... I've detested you.

17:41.602 --> 17:45.981
Then why don't you let it out,
if you detest me?

17:47.191 --> 17:48.192
Dad...

17:49.109 --> 17:52.404
What you're saying is crazy.
We're father and son, you know.

17:52.488 --> 17:56.033
If you and I were to fight,
Dad, it wouldn't be a match.

17:56.825 --> 18:02.664
Both agreeing to it, getting into
top form by a set date and time...

18:02.748 --> 18:04.041
It wouldn't be like that.

18:04.124 --> 18:06.794
As we live as father and son,

18:06.877 --> 18:08.796
one random day in our everyday life...

18:09.671 --> 18:14.551
a trivial thing, a truly trivial thing
causes us to start a small argument.

18:15.427 --> 18:17.554
Eventually it turns into a quarrel

18:18.138 --> 18:20.474
and ultimately,
the animosity we've suppressed...

18:22.559 --> 18:23.811
I see.

18:23.894 --> 18:25.312
Yes, I see.

18:25.896 --> 18:28.148
It may be just as you say.

18:30.776 --> 18:32.069
By the way, my son...

18:33.403 --> 18:34.822
<i>It's happening already?!</i>

18:35.405 --> 18:39.409
What the hell is your problem
serving me this crappy coffee?

18:41.912 --> 18:44.081
<i>There it is. That was sudden!</i>

18:44.665 --> 18:48.794
<i>An unnaturally trivial trigger.</i>

18:50.087 --> 18:51.380
I am very sorry, Father.

18:55.968 --> 18:58.595
Even though you came all the way here,

18:59.388 --> 19:02.099
I heedlessly served you terrible coffee.

19:03.600 --> 19:06.687
I'll be more careful from now on.
I beg your forgiveness.

19:10.482 --> 19:12.359
Come on, Dad.

19:12.442 --> 19:14.361
Don't go lying to me.

19:15.946 --> 19:20.617
No matter how trivial,
it needs to be a real problem.

19:22.661 --> 19:24.621
You drank it in just two gulps.

19:24.705 --> 19:27.624
So the coffee was actually good.

19:29.459 --> 19:31.879
Like it or not,

19:32.504 --> 19:36.884
family harmony doesn't interest me
in the least, and I can't understand it.

19:37.467 --> 19:38.510
That is all.

19:40.721 --> 19:41.597
Dad.

19:44.224 --> 19:45.684
Make me some coffee.

19:48.729 --> 19:51.231
Come on. It's not too much to ask, right?

19:52.232 --> 19:54.526
I'd like to drink coffee you've made, Dad.

19:59.239 --> 20:02.910
You can have coffee made by Yujiro Hanma.

20:05.746 --> 20:09.166
There is just one way you can have it.

20:10.500 --> 20:12.920
That's by forcing me to make it.

20:14.796 --> 20:18.175
Grab the reluctant Yujiro Hanma
by the scruff of the neck

20:20.010 --> 20:21.845
and force him to make it.

20:22.512 --> 20:23.931
If he refuses,

20:24.014 --> 20:27.935
slap him, knock him down, and punch him

20:28.018 --> 20:31.188
until he submits and makes it.

20:35.734 --> 20:37.194
Give him no option.

20:38.028 --> 20:40.280
You'll have to force him.

20:43.033 --> 20:44.284
If you can do that, Baki,

20:45.786 --> 20:47.704
you can even make him cook for you!

20:53.043 --> 20:56.964
<i>His father's words and the table
that had been broken into four pieces,</i>

20:57.547 --> 20:59.675
<i>he turned these things over in his mind.</i>

20:59.758 --> 21:02.469
<i>Wow, that was easy.</i>

21:04.972 --> 21:08.225
<i>Do I feel relieved?</i>

21:08.308 --> 21:10.185
<i>Baki was astonished.</i>

21:10.936 --> 21:15.232
<i>When his father, Yujiro Hanma,
the man he must overcome, left,</i>

21:16.024 --> 21:19.236
<i>he clearly felt relieved.</i>

21:20.070 --> 21:21.989
Dad!

21:25.826 --> 21:26.743
What's wrong?

21:26.827 --> 21:27.995
You want coffee?

21:29.413 --> 21:30.580
The front door...

21:32.833 --> 21:34.251
You need to shut it gently.

21:38.964 --> 21:40.757
You're exactly right.

21:45.971 --> 21:50.892
<i>Inside Baki's mind, a single phrase
whirled around at high speed.</i>

21:52.394 --> 21:55.188
<i>Telling him to come and close it again
would be going too far.</i>

21:56.648 --> 21:59.318
<i>Telling your father to do that
would be going too far.</i>

22:00.068 --> 22:01.737
<i>This is far enough.</i>

